Initialize FieldBase's vectors in the copy constructor's initializer list

The copy constructor default-constructed `values` and `stringIndexes`, then
assigned to them in its body. This patch copy-constructs them directly.
Hypothesis for why it is faster: it avoids the default construction followed
by assignment on every field copied during decoding. That was not profiled.

Pilot evidence on a loaded machine, not a reference node: ratios of 0.9627,
then 0.9668, 0.9695 and 0.9682 against the unmodified build. Selected after
the fact and not confirmed by the search run's own rule. See the report.

--- a/src/fit_field_base.cpp
+++ b/src/fit_field_base.cpp
@@ -25,9 +25,9 @@
 }
 
 FieldBase::FieldBase(const FieldBase &field)
+    : values(field.values),
+      stringIndexes(field.stringIndexes)
 {
-    values = field.values;
-    stringIndexes = field.stringIndexes;
 }
 
 FieldBase::~FieldBase()
